"""
Macro Research Platform - Institutional Dashboard

Professional hedge fund-style macro regime research dashboard.
Uses modular UI components from src/ui/.

Run with:
    streamlit run dashboard.py

# =============================================================================
# CHANGE SUMMARY
# =============================================================================
# FIXED: Replaced all print() statements with logging.info() calls
# FIXED: Replaced all bare `except:` with `except Exception:` to avoid
#        swallowing KeyboardInterrupt / SystemExit
# FIXED: latest_date > current_date comparison now uses pd.Timestamp for safety
# FIXED: days_warning_html hex-color inline rgba crash — safe_hex_to_rgb()
#        helper now guards against rgba() or short hex strings
# FIXED: st.sidebar.button() calls with invalid `width='stretch'` kwarg replaced
#        with use_container_width=True
# FIXED: st.button() theme toggle with invalid `width='stretch'` kwarg replaced
#        with use_container_width=True
# FIXED: st.dataframe() debug panel with invalid `width='stretch'` kwarg replaced
#        with use_container_width=True
# FIXED: latest_date timezone-awareness: strip tzinfo before comparing to
#        datetime.now() so the subtraction never raises TypeError
# FIXED: DATA_MODE hard-coded default "sample" caused dashboard to display
#        sample-data scores while latest_model_results.json was generated from
#        live data, producing a visible mismatch (e.g. inflation score -1.13 in
#        sample vs +1.07 in live JSON → regime label "Inflation Pressure" was
#        contradicted by the displayed score).  Now auto-detects "live" if
#        data/processed/live/macro_data.parquet exists on disk.
# FIXED: sector model call in load_and_process() used credit_stress_score=0.0
#        (hardcoded) and financial_conditions="neutral" (default), ignoring
#        actual tightening/easing conditions.  Now passes fc_impulse derived
#        from liquidity direction and recession_prob as a decimal fraction.
# FIXED: recession_prob was computed AFTER the sector model call, so the model
#        always received recession_prob=0.0 (the default).  Moved recession_prob
#        calculation to before the sector model call.
# =============================================================================
"""

